        <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked <span class="accent">Questions</span></h2>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Is GridPaw free to play?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">Yes, GridPaw is completely free to play in your browser. There is no download, no account, and no payment required. Just open the page and start solving.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>What is an Akari (Light Up) puzzle?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">Akari, also called Light Up, is a Japanese logic puzzle where you place lights so every empty cell is illuminated, while numbered cells tell you exactly how many adjacent lights they touch. GridPaw is the cat-themed version — place glowing cats instead of bulbs!</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>How is GridPaw different from Sudoku?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">Both are logic puzzles, but the rules are very different. Sudoku fills a grid with numbers; GridPaw places glowing cats to light up the board. If you like Sudoku's deduction, you'll enjoy GridPaw's clue-based lighting. The spatial reasoning is a refreshing change from number crunching.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Where should beginners start?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">Start with the Tutorial level, which walks you through every rule step by step, then move to Easy 5×5 boards before trying bigger grids. Check our <a href="/how-to-play/">How to Play</a> guide for a complete walkthrough.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Is there a GridPaw mobile app?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">Yes, GridPaw is available on Google Play, and the web version works on any device with a browser. The grid is fully responsive — long-press cells to mark them with paw prints on mobile.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Does my progress save automatically?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">Yes, your progress, lives, and current level are saved automatically in your browser via local storage, so you can come back and continue anytime on the same device.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>What do the numbered black cells mean?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">Each number tells you exactly how many of the 4 adjacent cells (up, down, left, right) must contain a cat. A "0" means none, a "4" means all four. Unnumbered black cells are just walls — they block light but give no clues.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Can I create my own puzzles?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">Yes! Visit the <a href="/create/">Create Puzzle</a> page to design your own Akari grid. The tool validates that your puzzle has exactly one solution, then generates a shareable link.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Does GridPaw have a daily challenge?</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">Yes! A fresh 10×10 puzzle is generated every day, and weekends (Sat & Sun UTC) feature a 14×14 Weekend Super Challenge. Track your solving streak and earn badges at 3, 7, 14, and 30 consecutive days. Visit the <a href="/daily/">Daily Challenge</a> page to play today's puzzle.</div>
        </details>
